        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Problem — part one: the extension is the launcher"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This is the seventh gap, the structural one the story adds to the six measured during bring-up.",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "strong"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "docs/SETUP.md",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " reads as if the daemon begins at §6 (line 314), "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\"Autostart, and the file-descriptor ceiling\"",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "em"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", which runs "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "install-service.sh",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " and ends with "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "systemctl --user enable --now butchr-daemon.service",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". Nothing before §6 says a daemon is running."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "It is not true. The native-messaging host is a launcher: Chrome spawns it when the extension connects, and it brings the daemon up if one is not already there. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "daemon/src/native-host.ts",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ":"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "codeBlock",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "127: // Connect (and spawn the daemon if needed) as soon as Chrome starts us, so\n128: // the first real message doesn't pay the startup latency.\n129: void ensureDaemonLink();"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "So §4 — \"Load the extension into Chrome\" — starts the daemon.",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "strong"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " Two consequences the document does not carry:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletList",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A box cannot be staged \"ready but inert\" by withholding §6.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "strong"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " An operator who wants everything installed but nothing running has no such state available by stopping short, and the document implies they do."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "This is the same mechanism as the KAN-550 incident §7 already describes",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "strong"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", from the other end. §7 (line 441) says that on 2026-08-20 "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "systemctl is-active",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "code"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " read "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "inactive",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "code"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " while "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "\"a daemon Chrome had auto-spawned served the fleet with none of the unit's `BUTCHR_",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "em"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " variables\"*. §7 explains how ",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "code"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "butchr-doctor` now catches that. It never says "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "why Chrome had a daemon to auto-spawn in the first place",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "strong"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " — which is this gap. The reader gets the remedy without the cause."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Problem — part two: §9's warning is narrower than the rule it is an instance of"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "§9 (line 519) warns, correctly and at length, that turning channels on does not reach agents that are already running: "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\"whether an agent has a channel is decided when it is spawned\"",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "em"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", and "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\"Those agents are deaf for the rest of their lives and the daemon will keep writing frames at them.\"",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "em"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "That is written as a fact about channels. It is an instance of a general rule: "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "a daemon-side switch never changes what an already-connected client negotiated.",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "strong"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " It is true of the Atlassian proxy in exactly the same way — flipping "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "BUTCHR_ATLASSIAN_PROXY",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " does not give an already-running agent the tools it did not have when its MCP session was negotiated."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "task/KAN-568",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " proposed "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "generalising §9's warning rather than adding a proxy footnote",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "strong"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", and KAN-612 endorses that as the better fix. A footnote per switch is a list that will be incomplete the day a switch is added; the rule is what survives."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
