              "type": "text",
              "text": " §4 and §5. This is the one genuine overlap in the three-way split. Read that sibling's merged text before you write yours, put your sentence where its ordering leaves room, and if the two cannot both be true, say so on this ticket and to "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "story/KAN-612",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "strong"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " rather than editing around it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "attrs": {
            "level": 2
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Standing rules"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletList",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Work lands as a pull request against protected "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "main",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "code"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ". Required CI checks must pass; read the current required set with "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "gh pr checks",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "code"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " rather than a remembered list, and filter by workflow ("
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "gh run list --workflow=ci.yml",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "code"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ") so you are not reading another workflow's conclusion."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Approval before merge, and green CI is not approval.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "strong"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " Your approver is "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "story/KAN-612",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "strong"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ". You merge your own PR, but only after that approval is on it."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Declare the approver in the PR body on a line of its own: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "BUTCHR-APPROVER: story/KAN-612",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "code"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ". The required "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "approval-recorded",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "code"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " check compares the approver's marker against that line, so a PR that declares nobody cannot go green."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "An approval is pinned to the head SHA. If you push or run "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "gh pr update-branch",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "code"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " after approval, the approval no longer names the head and you must ask again."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
